==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|he|en}} {{m|he|יִשְׁמָעֵאל||God hears, God will hear|tr=yishma'él (yišmāʿēl)}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|Abrahamic religions}} The eldest [[son]] of [[Abraham]] and his wife's handmaiden [[Hagar]] who were cast out after the [[birth]] of [[Isaac]]; [[traditionally]] the [[ancestor]] of the [[Arab]]s via the [[Ishmaelites]].
#* '''1611''' — [[w:King James Version of the Bible|King James Version of the Bible]], ''[[s:Bible (King James)/Genesis|Genesis]] 16:15''
#*: And Hagar bare Abram a son: and Abram called his son's name, which Hagar bare, '''Ishmael'''.
# {{given name|en|male|from=Hebrew}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1851|author={{w|Herman Melville}}|title=[[s:Moby-Dick|Moby-Dick]]|chapter=1|passage=Call me '''Ishmael'''.}}
# {{lb|en|type}} An outcast.
#* '''1932''' [[Frank Richards|The Magnet - Bunter's Night Out]]
#*: His new friend was evidently a young '''Ishmael''' - his hand against every man and every man's hand against him.

